{"id":"zeitplan","lemma":"Zeitplan","pos":"noun","rank":3998,"glosses":["timetable, schedule"],"audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/16/De-Zeitplan.ogg/De-Zeitplan.ogg.mp3","gender":"m","forms":{"genitive":"Zeitplanes","plural":"Zeitpläne"},"examples":[{"text":"Hat sich unser Zeitplan geändert?","en":"Has our schedule changed?","words":[{"g":"has","l":"haben"},{"g":"oneself"},{"g":"our"},null,{"g":"changed"}]},{"text":"Mein Zeitplan ist ziemlich voll.","en":"My schedule is rather tight.","words":[{"g":"my"},null,{"g":"is","l":"sein"},{"g":"pretty"},{"g":"full"}]},{"text":"Wir liegen im Zeitplan.","en":"We're on schedule.","words":[{"g":"we"},{"g":"to lie"},{"g":"in the"},null]},{"text":"Ich bin schon hinter dem Zeitplan.","en":"I'm running behind schedule.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"am","l":"sein"},{"g":"already"},{"g":"behind, after"},{"g":"(to) the","l":"der"},null]},{"text":"Jedenfalls können wir den Zeitplan nicht ändern.","en":"At any rate, we can't change the schedule.","words":[{"g":"in any case"},{"g":"can, to be able to"},{"g":"we"},{"g":"the","l":"der"},null,{"g":"not"},{"g":"to change, to alter"}]}]}